# Astro

Apply only in Astro projects. Prefer project conventions over inventing structure.

## Defaults

- Prefer pure Astro components (`.astro`) for presentational UI.
- Type component props with TypeScript (`Props` interface / `Astro.props`).
- Avoid React, Vue, Svelte, or other UI frameworks unless explicitly requested.
- Avoid client-side JavaScript when HTML/CSS can achieve the same behavior.
- Prefer server-rendered or statically generated HTML.
- Separate layouts, components, pages, content, and utilities.

## Practices

- Follow Atomic Design and the section wrapper → container → column pattern.
- Colocate styles with components unless the project uses a shared stylesheet/token system.
- Use official Astro APIs; do not invent framework features or rely on outdated APIs.
- Consult project `AGENTS.md` and [Astro docs](https://docs.astro.build) when unsure.

## Anti-patterns

- Shipping unnecessary `client:*` directives.
- Mixing CMS fetch logic into presentational atoms.
- Duplicating layout primitives per page.
